From 71994e66e7719bcdcbddcac6303f6a83b638208f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gigi <42325924+g-cqd@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 22:46:27 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] fix(airconv): output the varyings a pixel shader reads
 from a GS mesh pipeline

D3D11 links stages by register and leaves a pixel shader input that the
geometry shader does not write undefined. DXMT emitted only the GS's
declared outputs as mesh vertex data, and on M1/M2 (G14X) Apple's compiler
crashes on a mesh pipeline whose fragment function reads a varying missing
from the mesh outputs (null Value in AGCLLVMUserMeshShaderSW::getBasePointer;
"Failed to create mesh PSO: ... XPC_ERROR_CONNECTION_INTERRUPTED"). Crysis 3
does this; the effect was lost (before: GPU fault and hang).

The GS variant now depends on the pixel shader (ShaderVariantGeometry,
new compilation argument SM50_SHADER_PSO_PIXEL_SHADER_INPUT, also converted
for 32-bit callers). The pixel shader records its user inputs while it is
parsed; the GS converter adds a mesh output for each one the GS does not
output: the GS output register with the element's components when the GS
declares that register, otherwise zero. Converters that do not know the
argument ignore it.

In a sweep over the 736 shaders Crysis 3 had in the DXMT cache, all 344
compiler crashes were such pairs (0 of 1692 linked pairs crashed).
tests/dx11/dx11_failed_pipeline gs mode: before, the pipeline fails and the
draw is dropped; after, it compiles and renders exactly green (TEXCOORD1
zero), i686 and x86_64. A ts mode (one patch at tess factor 64) is added
as a smoke test of the tessellation path.
